PARITY SUMMARY
  The web XRayControls is a controls bar (flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4) of three constrained <Select>s:
    1. Vehicle  (w-64) : vehicleOptions = { '', t('admin.xray.controls.selectVehicle','Select vehicle…') }
                         + one option per vehicle, label = v.display_name || v.vin || `Vehicle ${v.id}`.
                         aria-label = t('admin.xray.controls.vehicleAria','Vehicle'); '' → onVehicleChange(null).
    2. Window   (w-40) : windowOptions = ALL_WINDOWS.map(w => t(`admin.xray.windowOption.${w}`, w))  [fallback=raw token]
    3. Bucket   (w-40) : bucketOptions = ALL_BUCKETS.map(b => ({ t(`admin.xray.bucketOption.${b}`, b),
                         disabled: BUCKET_SECS[b] >= WINDOW_SECS[windowSel] }))  — the `tooBig` guard that
                         pre-empts a server-side "bucket >= window" 400.
  Native port reproduces ALL of it: the empty vehicle sentinel + per-vehicle label fallback chain (empty strings
  treated as absent, matching JS `||`), every window/bucket option with the RAW-TOKEN web fallback and the exact
  t() keys, and the BUCKET_SECS>=WINDOW_SECS disable guard (boundary inclusive: a 1h bucket in a 1h window is
  disabled). WINDOW_SECS/BUCKET_SECS match the web maps exactly. The web `Select` maps to a native `Menu` with a
  bordered field trigger and one `Button` per option (checkmark on the selected, `.disabled` on `tooBig` buckets) —
  the Apple-idiomatic equivalent of an HTML <select> with disabled <option>s (a plain SwiftUI Picker cannot disable
  individual rows). The responsive flex-wrap maps to ViewThatFits(.horizontal): single row when wide, stacked
  column when compact. IngestXRayWindow is OWNED by the sibling XRayHeader surface and REUSED verbatim (same target,
  not redefined); IngestXRayBucket + XRayVehicleRef are introduced here. Data binds through XRayControlsModel
  (P1/S8 seam mirroring LoadableState / LiveConnectionState); the bar reports selections through the source
  (web controlled-component onVehicleChange/onWindowChange/onBucketChange) — no HTTP in the view. P1/S11
  view.opened telemetry fires once on appear with slug "XRayControls".

STATES (every state renders — none hidden behind a null guard)
  The vehicle list is the loadable the picker depends on; its lifecycle drives the vehicle slot, while the
  window + bucket selectors (pure operator selections) stay usable in EVERY state.
  loading  → vehicle slot = field-shaped shimmer skeleton; window+bucket live.
  content  → populated vehicle picker; window+bucket live.
  empty    → disabled vehicle picker (the "Select vehicle…" sentinel) + a friendly "no vehicles yet" hint,
             never a blank box; window+bucket live.
  error    → inline QueryError-equivalent in the vehicle slot + Retry (model.refresh); window+bucket live.
  stale    → freshness banner ("the vehicle list may be stale") + cached picker + one auto-refresh on entering stale.
  offline  → freshness banner ("showing the last loaded vehicles") + cached picker.

